From d94c96a151f70c2ef5be7395a23b6847d2f335bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:40:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] [AGS] Fix three residual Phase D gaps found continuing
 the build past 0023

Three real, previously-unreached gaps found by continuing make build-ags
past patch 0023, each independently diagnosed and narrow -- not one
concern repeated, three distinct root causes, bundled here because each
was found and fixed within the same continued-build investigation and
each is a single line:

- Engine/media/video/videoplayer.h:171: SDL_AudioFormat _audioFormat = 0;
  SDL_AudioFormat is a plain Uint16 typedef in SDL2 (implicit int init
  compiles fine) but a real C++ enum in SDL3 (implicit int init is a
  hard -fpermissive-only error under this build's flags). Fixed to
  SDL_AUDIO_UNKNOWN. This header is not excluded by AGS_NO_VIDEO_PLAYER
  the way theora_player.cpp's own decode source is -- Engine/ac/game.cpp
  pulls it in unconditionally via media/video/video.h -- so it needed
  fixing regardless of video playback ever being exercised. Breadth-
  checked: grepped the whole tree for every SDL_[A-Za-z_]+ member
  initialized to a bare `= 0` and checked each type against SDL3's real
  enums vs. plain bitmask typedefs (e.g. SDL_WindowFlags, still Uint64,
  correctly `= 0` in sys_main.cpp) -- this is the only real instance.

- Engine/ac/global_game.cpp: extends patch 0017's own coverage, not a
  fresh unrelated finding. GetPressedKeys() calls .size()/operator[] on
  the std::vector<SDL_KeyboardEvent>& ags_getkeysdown() returns (already
  ported by 0017), but sys_events.h only forward-declares
  `struct SDL_KeyboardEvent;` (by design, to stay a light header) --
  instantiating vector<T>::size()/operator[] needs T complete at the
  point of use, which requires global_game.cpp itself to include the
  real definition. Added #include <SDL3/SDL.h> (pulls in SDL_events.h,
  where SDL_KeyboardEvent's full struct actually lives, confirmed by
  reading SDL_events.h:360 directly) -- 0017's own patch happened not to
  need this for the sites it touched directly, but this call site does.

- Engine/ac/room.cpp: a new instance of the established DJGPP
  int32_t/uint32_t-vs-int/unsigned-int divergence category (patches
  0013/0018/0019's own category, here on the unsigned side): DJGPP's
  uint32_t is `unsigned long`, not `unsigned int` (confirmed with a
  static_assert probe), so Math::Clamp<T>'s single-template-parameter
  deduction fails when a uint32_t variable, a bare `0u` literal
  (unsigned int), and a uint32_t-typed expression are all passed as the
  three same-T arguments -- GCC reports "no matching function," listing
  the mismatched deduced types. Fixed both call sites in
  convert_move_path_to_data_resolution() with an explicit
  Math::Clamp<uint32_t>(...) template argument, matching the existing
  precedent already used for exactly this shape at
  Engine/ac/listbox.cpp:323 (Math::Clamp<uint32_t>(item, 0u, ...)) --
  not inventing a new pattern.

Verified: videoplayer.h via Engine/ac/game.cpp.obj (the file that pulls
it in); global_game.cpp.obj and room.cpp.obj directly. All three compile
clean, zero errors. Full make build-ags / cmake --build ... -- -k
(keep-going) re-run: no new errors from these three files anywhere in
the build.
---
 Engine/ac/global_game.cpp        | 1 +
 Engine/ac/room.cpp               | 4 ++--
 Engine/media/video/videoplayer.h | 2 +-
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Engine/ac/global_game.cpp b/Engine/ac/global_game.cpp
index 09a474711..8a035f621 100644
--- a/Engine/ac/global_game.cpp
+++ b/Engine/ac/global_game.cpp
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
